# Docs sync

HydraHook documentation lives in this repository. There are no HydraHook pages on docs.nefarius.at.

When a change is user-facing or changes the architecture described in a README, update the matching doc in the same change:

| Source | Doc |
|---|---|
| `include/HydraHook/**` public API | Doxygen comments, `README.md`, `src/HydraHook/README.md` |
| `src/HydraHook/**` engine, hooks, shutdown | `src/HydraHook/README.md` |
| `samples/**` | `samples/README.md` and `samples/<sample>/README.md` |
| `vcpkg.json` | `README.md` dependency and build steps |
| `.github/workflows/**` | `README.md` build, test, and release sections |
| `tests/**` | `README.md` Tests section and `src/HydraHook/README.md` Testing section |

Pure formatting or comment-only edits do not need a doc update.
